		"guide_text": "CONTROLS\n• Wheel: touch and rotate the circle on the left. It re-centres when released.\n• GAS and BRAKE are levers: slide to a level and PAUSE before lifting to fix it there (yellow handle). A quick flick is a \"tap\" that fades to 0 in about half a second. Slide down to reduce; the bottom is 0. Low brake = light, high = hard; touching the brake resets the gas.\n• Automatic: P (park) · R (reverse) · N (neutral) · D (drive). The car creeps in D/R when you release the brake.\n• Manual: hold CLUTCH and tap up/down to shift. Releasing the clutch at low speed without gas stalls the engine, press START to restart.\n• Left/right signals, hazard lights (triangle), HORN, LIGHT, H.BRAKE, BELT, CAM (switch view).\n\nTEST SCORING\n• Start with 100 points, pass with 80 or more and no disqualification.\n• Wheel on boundary line: −5 each time. Leaving the course: disqualified.\n• Engine over 4,000 rpm: −2. Stall: −5.\n• Stop past the line or more than 50 cm before it: −5. Not stopping: disqualified.\n• Red light: −10. No signal at start/finish: −5.\n• Parking: not in the bay: disqualified; over 2 minutes: −5.\n• Emergency: hazards on within 3 s and stop, otherwise −10.\n\nTIPS\n• Drive at 5–10 km/h on the course and use the mirrors when reversing.\n• Press CAM for an outside view while learning.",
